From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:18:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] tests: pass, fail and boundary for every veto; the
 holdout lock by name

Each veto gets all three cases, because a threshold written < instead of <= is
a silent permanent change to the mandate. lookahead and frequency are tested
against the synthetic panel's known break dates and against the real mistake,
treating real_date as the knowledge date. The holdout tests assert no bypass
argument exists in any signature.
